{"html":"<p>Rust is not replacing JavaScript on the web. It is replacing the <em>hot 5%</em> of a\nweb app — the part where the frame budget is spent.</p>\n<h2 id=\"what-the-domain-demands\">What the domain demands</h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Requirement</th>\n<th>Consequence</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>16 ms per frame</td>\n<td>Any per-frame allocation shows up as jank</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>No blocking the main thread</td>\n<td>Long tasks kill interaction and Core Web Vitals</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Deterministic memory</td>\n<td>Mobile Safari will kill a tab over ~200 MB</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Ship over the wire</td>\n<td>Bundle size is a product decision, not a detail</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Run everywhere</td>\n<td>One artifact for browser, edge worker and server</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<h2 id=\"who-runs-it\">Who runs it</h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Product</th>\n<th>How Rust is used</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Figma</strong></td>\n<td>the multiplayer engine and parts of the renderer are compiled to WebAssembly; Figma published the work on getting a 3× speedup from the wasm rewrite</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Shopify</strong></td>\n<td>\"Functions\" — merchant business logic compiled to WebAssembly and run inside Shopify's infrastructure</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Discord</strong></td>\n<td>the desktop client's voice/video and some client services are Rust; the Read States service rewrite removed GC pauses</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>1Password</strong></td>\n<td>a shared Rust core powering the crypto and data layer across every platform</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Cloudflare Workers</strong></td>\n<td>Rust targets the edge runtime; the worker runs in a V8 isolate with wasm</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Every JS bundler</strong></td>\n<td>swc, Turbopack and Biome are Rust programs doing the work webpack did in JS</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>The common thread: the code that had to be fast, or had to be <em>identical</em> on five\nplatforms, moved to Rust. The UI layer stayed where it was.</p>\n<h2 id=\"the-shape-of-the-code\">The shape of the code</h2>\n<p>A wasm module is a function library, not an application. Design its boundary\nfirst.</p>\n<figure data-rehype-pretty-code-figure=\"\"><pre tabindex=\"0\" data-language=\"rust\" data-theme=\"github-light github-dark-dimmed\"><code data-language=\"rust\" data-theme=\"github-light github-dark-dimmed\" style=\"display: grid;\"><span data-line=\"\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\">use</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#F69D50\"> wasm_bindgen</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\">::</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#F69D50\">prelude</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\">::*</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">;</span></span>\n<span data-line=\"\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\">use</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#F69D50\"> serde</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\">::</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">{</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#F69D50\">Deserialize</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">, </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#F69D50\">Serialize</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">};</span></span>\n<span data-line=\"\"> </span>\n<span data-line=\"\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">#[derive(</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#F69D50\">Serialize</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">, </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#F69D50\">Deserialize</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">)]</span></span>\n<span data-line=\"\"><span styl